{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And he who comes to whom the house belongs.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in the first chapter of Yoma: one whose house is uniquely his — that is, he does not wish to lend his utensils or does not bring guests into his house — for afflictions come upon the stingy (צרות עין), and this is what it says: <b>and he who comes to whom the house belongs</b> shall come and tell the priest, saying, <b>something like a plague appears to me in the house</b>." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> <b>And he who comes to whom the house belongs</b> — this is the Holy One, blessed be He; <b>and he shall tell the priest</b> — this is Jeremiah; <b>something like a plague appears to me in the house</b> — this is the idol that Manasseh set up in the sanctuary."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:19.448714151Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}